        "id": 1139038
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-02T17:43:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can\u0027t actually apply this set of rules in VTS because it could be a ROM that shipped with a valid implementation against VSR 14 but had a software update to VSR 15, but obviously the ROM isn\u0027t going to update.\n\nIn VSR 16 we\u0027re going to add a DICE profile version which will let us handle this in future.\n\nI also think the translation of API level to VSR / ruleset should move inside hwtrust so each client doesn\u0027t have to deal with the translation.",
      "revId": "4df23e605d754560f5a489fa0bab7de73ae377bf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "48175f20_d0987e0a",
        "filename": "security/keymint/support/remote_prov_utils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 938,
      "author": {
        "id": 1833664
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-02T17:58:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Isn\u0027t `ro.vendor.api_level` going to be fixed, though?\n\nA ROM that cannot support a higher VSR cannot be updated to that VSR, right? Perhaps I miss your point.",
      "parentUuid": "3d511747_aa6610ef",
      "revId": "4df23e605d754560f5a489fa0bab7de73ae377bf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "57b89453_cb33c206",
        "filename": "security/keymint/support/remote_prov_utils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 938,
      "author": {
        "id": 1139038
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-02T18:07:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That has proved to be too restrictive a policy for SoCs. We were saying \"you\u0027re stuck with Android 14 because of a little data format change for RKP\" which does seem like a bit of an out-weighted influence.",
      "parentUuid": "48175f20_d0987e0a",
      "revId": "4df23e605d754560f5a489fa0bab7de73ae377bf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "656bc062_e712fb78",
        "filename": "security/keymint/support/remote_prov_utils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 938,
      "author": {
        "id": 1833664
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-02T21:03:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Capturing offline discussion here:\n\nMy perspective is that even for different VSR levels we need to account for ROM that may be \"stuck\" with some quirks. This means that even if VSR 15 is more strict on some things, we may only be able to apply that strictness to firmware that can be updated to match the VSR.\n\nIn practice I think this means validation of the first DICE chain entry is going to be more lenient than the rest of the chain, as the ROM measurement is always the first entry.\n\nI cannot imagine a case where ROM records multiple DICE chain entries (though I guess anything is possible?). We can always deal with that edge case if/when it does occur.",
      "parentUuid": "57b89453_cb33c206",
      "revId": "4df23e605d754560f5a489fa0bab7de73ae377bf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2bb0b7b2_c58329e1",
        "filename": "security/keymint/support/remote_prov_utils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 938,
      "author": {
        "id": 1115498
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-03T10:10:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e In practice I think this means validation of the first DICE chain entry is going to be more lenient than the rest of the chain, as the ROM measurement is always the first entry.\n\nThe problem isn\u0027t the first entry though, it\u0027s the following entries. Some of our vendor partners bake their DICE library directly into their ROM mask, which will carry any inconsistencies into future firmware releases as well.\n\nI don\u0027t think we can be any more strict about DICE format enforcement until we have a concept of a DICE version.",
      "parentUuid": "656bc062_e712fb78",
      "revId": "4df23e605d754560f5a489fa0bab7de73ae377bf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
